.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-3.0-or-later
.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt NQSIGNMU 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqsmu ,
.Nm nqsignmu ,
.Nm nqvrfymu
.Nd ML-DSA with an external message representative
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqsmu
.Fa "nqsalg alg"
.Fa "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *msg" "size_t msglen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *ctx" "size_t ctxlen" "int ph"
.Fa "uint8_t *mu" "size_t mulen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqsignmu
.Fa "nqsalg alg"
.Fa "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *mu" "size_t mulen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *rnd" "size_t rndlen"
.Fa "uint8_t *sig" "size_t siglen" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqvrfymu
.Fa "nqsalg alg"
.Fa "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *mu" "size_t mulen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *sig" "size_t siglen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
FIPS 204 lets the message representative
.Em mu ,
64 bytes of SHAKE256 over the hash of the public key, the domain and
context prefix and the message, be computed apart from the signer
(Algorithm 7, line 6, and Algorithm 8, line 7): a message can be hashed
where it is, and only
.Em mu
travel to the key.
These functions are that interface, for
.Dv NQMLDSA44 ,
.Dv NQMLDSA65
and
.Dv NQMLDSA87
only; SLH-DSA, Ed25519 and the hybrids have none
.Pq Dv NQENOSUP .
.Pp
.Fn nqsmu
writes
.Em mu
for the public key
.Fa pk ,
the message and the context
.Fa ctx
(at most 255 bytes) to
.Fa mu ,
.Fa mulen
being
.Dv NQMU
(64): pure ML-DSA with
.Fa ph
0, HashML-DSA with
.Fa ph
an
.Vt nqhalg ,
as in
.Xr nqsign 3 .
In symbols, with M the message, x the context, PH the hash
.Fa ph
names, OID(PH) the 11-byte DER encoding of its object identifier
06 09 60 86 48 01 65 03 04 02 nn, and
.Sy ||
concatenation:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
tr = SHAKE256(pk, 64)
M' = 0x00 || |x| || x || M                     ph 0
M' = 0x01 || |x| || x || OID(PH) || PH(M)      ph a hash
mu = SHAKE256(tr || M', 64)
.Ed
.Pp
where |x| is one byte, PH(M) is 32 bytes for SHAKE128 and 64 for
SHAKE256 (FIPS 204 Algorithm 4), and the signer's own
.Em mu
uses the tr stored in its secret key instead.
.Pp
.Fn nqsignmu
signs
.Em mu
with the secret key
.Fa sk
(first-order masked, as
.Fn nqsign ) .
.Fa rnd
is
.Dv NULL
with
.Fa rndlen
0 for the hedged signature (32 fresh bytes from
.Xr nqrand 3 ) ,
or 32 bytes (all zero for the deterministic variant).
The signature on the
.Em mu
of
.Fn nqsmu
is the one
.Fn nqsignd
gives for the same message, context, pre-hash and
.Fa rnd ,
byte for byte, and is checked under the public key computed from
.Fa sk
(t = A s1 + s2 from rho, s1 and s2) before it is returned.
.Pp
.Fn nqvrfymu
checks
.Fa sig
against
.Em mu
and
.Fa pk ;
it accepts exactly the signatures
.Fn nqvrfy
accepts for the message
.Em mu
came from.
.Pp
Nothing ties
.Em mu
to a message: whoever hands
.Em mu
to the signer decides what is signed.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK ,
or
.Bl -tag -width NQENOSUP
.It Bq Er NQEARG
An unknown
.Fa alg ,
a
.Dv NULL
pointer, a
.Fa mulen
other than 64, a context over 255 bytes, an unknown
.Fa ph ,
or an
.Fa rnd
of another length.
.It Bq Er NQEBUF
.Fa siglen
is smaller than the signature.
.It Bq Er NQEDEC
A key or signature of the wrong length, or a malformed one.
.It Bq Er NQEVRFY
The signature does not verify.
.It Bq Er NQEFLT
The new signature failed the check made after signing; it was wiped.
.It Bq Er NQENOSUP
.Fa alg
is a signature algorithm of noqtis other than an ML-DSA set (an
.Fa alg
noqtis does not know is
.Dv NQEARG ) .
.It Bq Er NQERNG
The random source failed.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
uint8_t mu[NQMU], sig[3309];
size_t n;
int rc = nqsmu(NQMLDSA65, pk, pklen, msg, msglen, NULL, 0, 0,
               mu, sizeof mu);
if (rc == NQOK)  /* elsewhere: only mu reaches the key */
  rc = nqsignmu(NQMLDSA65, sk, sklen, mu, sizeof mu, NULL, 0,
                sig, sizeof sig, &n);
if (rc == NQOK)
  rc = nqvrfy(NQMLDSA65, pk, pklen, msg, msglen, NULL, 0, 0, sig, n);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 3 ,
.Xr nqsign 3
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%T FIPS 204: Module-Lattice-Based Digital Signature Standard
.%Q NIST
.%D August 13, 2024
.Re
.Pp
The tests run every NIST ACVP ML-DSA sigGen and sigVer test with an
external mu through these functions.
